{"kind":"promise","text":"I will remove AddActor's duplicate kind vocabulary on request/legacy-roster-normalization, and nothing else.\n\nMy plan, so the shape is judgeable before I write it. The predicate both callers need is identical — is this word one of the descriptive kind words — and it already exists as RosterRoleIsKind, whose body is exactly right and whose name is not: it says role, and AddActor validates a kind. Two names for one predicate is the duplication in a different dress, so I intend one classifier named for the vocabulary rather than for either caller, used by both.\n\nThe subtle part is the second clause. Testing normalized.kind == word alone would admit the word unspecified, because the normalizer's default branch derives that kind for anything it does not recognise; the authorityRole empty clause is what excludes it, and the existing test already pins that. I will keep both clauses and keep that pin.\n\nThe drift test will tie AddActor's accepted set to the Workroom vocabulary rather than restate it, so adding a fourth kind in one place without the other fails. A test that lists human, agent and service again would pass happily while the two drifted, which is the whole defect.\n\nI will carry current main, run the focused app and workroom tests, the full suite, race, vet, build and diff-check, publish replacement exact-head artifacts for internal/app and internal/workroom, report, and request a fresh review from codex. I will not touch the normalization seam itself: I reviewed it, found it sound, and proved it by mutation.","body":{"branch":"request/legacy-roster-normalization"}}